%% D-14 Identity Flow
%% Source: docs/engineering/SECURITY_ARCHITECTURE.md; D-10-c4-container.mmd
%% Purpose: OIDC/Azure authentication, MFA, RBAC, and per-tenant session scoping (P3)

sequenceDiagram
    actor User as RTA Analyst
    participant SPA as Command Center SPA
    participant IdP as Azure / Entra ID (OIDC)
    participant Gateway as API Gateway
    participant Core as Rules Core / data

    User->>SPA: Open Command Center
    SPA->>IdP: Redirect - OIDC authorization-code request

    IdP->>User: Prompt for credentials
    User->>IdP: Submit credentials
    IdP->>User: MFA challenge (step-up for high-risk actions)
    User->>IdP: MFA response

    alt MFA fails
        IdP-->>SPA: Auth error
        SPA-->>User: Access denied
    else MFA succeeds
        IdP->>SPA: Authorization code
        SPA->>IdP: Exchange code for tokens (PKCE)
        IdP->>SPA: ID token + access token (claims: sub, roles, tenant_id)
        SPA->>SPA: Store token (session), no OIDC secret in browser

        SPA->>Gateway: API request + Bearer access token

        Gateway->>Gateway: Validate token (signature, expiry, issuer = Entra)
        Gateway->>Gateway: Check RBAC (role claim vs required permission)
        Gateway->>Gateway: Scope session to tenant_id claim (P3 - one tenant's data only)

        alt Token invalid or role lacks permission
            Gateway-->>SPA: 401 / 403
            SPA-->>User: Access denied
        else Token valid and RBAC passes
            Gateway->>Core: Forward request (tenant_id-scoped)
            Core-->>Gateway: Tenant-scoped data / CommandCard[]
            Gateway-->>SPA: Response
            SPA-->>User: Render cards (this tenant only)
        end
    end
